hello and welcome to my session about  zero effort analytical method validation  my name is jurgen fourgang and in the  next minutes i will show you  how this work flow can be implemented  selecting the ideal solution for today's  laboratories  this presentation will provide guidance  and show optimized workflows and tools  for selecting and implementing the ideal  method validation solution  that will save up to 70 percent of time  and cost  compared to performing the tasks  manually  as you can see the diagram 70 percent  can be saved  where the optimal workflow has been  implemented  what is important for the efficient  workflow we'll start with an overview  guidelines for method validation  analytical method validation work is  based on a variety of guidelines and  requirements  these guidelines define the basics of  validation work  the purpose the scope and what to do  we have lots of guidelines like ich  usp ep jp  dean iso fda and visa  and others  method validation work requires more  effort than ever  beginning with analytical and scientific  work  and even more reports and compliance  documentation  lots of paperwork reducing this work  and improving efficiency while ensuring  the highest level of documentation  quality  and data integrity is welcomed by both  qa and laboratory but how can this be  achieved  analytical method validation what do we  need for our work  the objective of the validation of an  analytical procedure  is to demonstrate that it is suitable  for its intended purpose  efficiency and data integrity are the  most important requirements for method  validation software solutions  but what does that mean and how can it  be achieved  first in terms of time from planning to  find a report  and second in terms of good and  compliant output  first efficiency in terms of time from  planning to final report  the workflow should be well defined  it is normally done in our sop document  easy to understand and easy to follow so  we need clear steps on the workflow  for creating a new project doing the  detailed planning and the project plan  entering our data either manually or by  using interfaces  and calculating and creating the final  result document  guided by wizards assistance and to-do  lists  so it's a very good idea to have a  software solution  with wizards and to-do lists that will  clearly offer what the next step would  be in the workflow  and eliminating the need to use  additional tools  no pocket calculator no excel no slide  rule  because all these external tools need to  be validated  and so in case you have one body data  tool  offering the complete workflow it is  good to stay with that tool  and to avoid aid external input  second efficiency in terms of good and  compliant output  a validated calculation framework is  mandatory  but we need more we need  result sets well-defined output with no  random changes  predefined layouts including your  corporate identity with logos  headers and cover pages predefined  summaries  that allow an easy summary of validation  projects main results  we need predefined formulas that can be  added to the report  to be much clearer how all these results  were  calculated but validation project should  not only contain calculations but all  data integrity related info  for full 21 civil party level compliance  data integrity full compliance to 2017  part 11 is mandatory  or to equivalent regulations like eu  gmp and x11 data protection can be  guaranteed by software access levels  by logins roles departments and check  some protected backend databases  like oracle or microsoft sql server  the whole workflow must be completely  tracked by means of  audit trades all activities in detail  as well as revision history both  searchable  and retrievable auditors have a very  close look on all aspects of electronic  data  so keep an eye on that it is very  important  21 cfr part 11. besides validation and  part 11 compliance certificates  a 21 cfr part 11 compliance response is  mandatory  this compliance response provides  detailed answers for the requirements of  part 11  it's a mandatory document when using a  software and regulated environments  it is part of your software  documentation as well as  iq and oq protocols and other quality  related paperwork  establishing an optimized workflow with  minimum effort  templates the key from optimized  workflow is predefining all  aspects of typical method validation  work by workflow templates  that reduce new projects to a few clicks  such templates follow your sops contain  typical workflows and workloads and  structure your tasks to optimize  efficiency and compliance communication  with your laboratory equipment  like cds lims ecm erp dms  should be automatic and easy with manual  intervention  limited to a minimum guidelines and  validation structure  guidelines are translated into  validation workload for example  checkpoints  to create and structure validation  projects  on the right side of the slide you can  see a typical validation project  it is organized as a hierarchical tree  with the name of the project on top  below that you can see the components or  chapters  and below them you can see the  individual checkpoints  the checkpoints have icons in front  which indicate  the status of the checkpoint it could be  unplanned planned containing data  or in case it's a traffic cloud symbol  it means  that acceptances were predefined  in the case of a red traffic light it  means that  at least one acceptance was not met and  green traffic light indicates  that everything is fine within this  checkpoint  testing workload your testing workload  is defined by your  accreditation authority customers sops  and your personal ambitions  in any case the testing workload must be  well-defined and not random  it must be clear why a specific workflow  as well as acceptance tracking has been  selected  this workflow definition is established  as a validation plan  that needs to be approved prior to  decoration start  custom workflows adopting  new or changed workflows should be as  easy as possible  graphical design tools business process  managers  allow user-designed workflows without  software modification  different projects require different  workflows that can be selected from  predefined designs more than result  calculation  documentation let's now focus on  documentation  method validation work is much more than  just calculating results  it is setting up your testing workload  both simple and flexible  with final documentation matching  customer expectations  as well as regulatory requirements  this requires a highly configurable and  powerful reporting solution  to create documentation templates for  all purposes  internal as well as official validation  reports  best practices important and frequently  used report elements should be available  for immediate usage  for example text blocks snippet  libraries  ease this process and guarantee good  reporting quality  this applies to headers approval  sections cover pages result acceptance  tables  and lots of other elements final  documentation  final method validation documentation  needs to be  easy to understand well structured  illustrated when necessary easily  summarized to get the main result  as you can see in these three examples  document transfer and protection fining  documents must follow established  standards for easy exchange  like pdfa standard and well protected by  secure algorithms  to be safe against external modification  integrate and embed your method  validation workflow into your lab  environment  interfacing your laboratory equipment  manual data input should be avoided  whenever possible  automatic transfer eliminates the need  to control and check manual inputs  all laboratory systems need to be  attached to your method validation  software like  cds chromatography data systems  lims lab information management system  erp enterprise resource planning  ecm enterprise content management  and dms document management system  interface workflow interfaces connect  your validation projects to external  data sources  these external sources can be easily  browsed  and the data used for your projects  data is automatically transferred  predefined workflows control data flow  and reduce time and eliminate input  errors  a typical workflow could be create  a new validation project connect it to a  data source  like cds lims erp or ecm  [Music]  assign and load the data and create the  final validation  report and export it in all the typical  formats like pdfa  when you're using that you will have a  highly integrated predefined workflow  that makes it easy to create a new  project  flexibility even a method validation  project based on a well-established  template  might need modifications for a specific  pending project  here we have three examples for that the  first one is a data input grid  with additional data columns the second  one  is a custom defined report output with a  detailed analysis of recovery data  and the third example is an additional  calculation script for having an  extended calculation workflow  project fine tuning while templates  define routine work it's critical to  allow flexibility for each new project  additional calculations graphics and  report extensions must be added easily  hence it is viable to allow fine-tuning  of your projects for specific purpose  for example different testing workflow  additional calculations or modified  layout  in any case such modifications must be  fully checked  the difference to the underlying  template explained  and justified in the validation plan  maximum level of data integrity  since your data is worth being protected  all this must be accompanied by a  maximum level of data integrity  which means strict access control  detailed traceability  version history and full 21 cfor part 11  compliance  centralized installations application  and database server  a